    "section_JTX7ii": {
      "type": "section",
      "blocks": {
        "text_LTKPD8": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.heading",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2>The early signs of | cardiovascular disease|</h2>",
            "width": "100%",
            "max_width": "normal",
            "alignment": "center",
            "type_preset": "custom",
            "font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
            "font_size": "2.375rem",
            "font_size_mobile": "1.5rem",
            "weight": "",
            "line_height": "tight",
            "letter_spacing": "normal",
            "case": "none",
            "wrap": "pretty",
            "text_color": "",
            "highlight_color": "#601c22",
            "background": false,
            "background_color": "#00000026",
            "corner_radius": 0,
            "padding-block-start": 0,
            "padding-block-end": 0,
            "padding-inline-start": 0,
            "padding-inline-end": 0
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "advanced_tabs_qYFWm9": {
          "type": "advanced-tabs",
          "name": "Advanced tabs",
          "settings": {
            "accessibility_label": "Tabbed content",
            "media_aspect_ratio": "16 / 9",
            "media_radius": 0,
            "tab_radius": 6,
            "tab_font_size": 16,
            "mobile_tab_font_size": 14,
            "heading_font_size": 34,
            "mobile_heading_font_size": 24,
            "text_font_size": 17,
            "mobile_text_font_size": 17,
            "note_font_size": 17,
            "mobile_note_font_size": 16,
            "color_text": "#555555",
            "color_heading": "#4e2b23",
            "color_accent": "#4e2b23",
            "color_active_text": "#ffffff",
            "color_background": "#ffffff",
            "gradient_background": "",
            "padding-block-start": 40,
            "padding-block-end": 72
          },
          "blocks": {
            "tab_HmVGNt": {
              "type": "_tab",
              "settings": {
                "tab_label": "Stage 1: Inflammation Damages the Artery Wall",
                "media_type": "image",
                "image": "shopify://shop_images/stage_1_natto.png",
                "show_play_icon": true,
                "video_url": "",
                "autoplay_video": false,
                "heading": "<strong>Stage 1: Inflammation Damages the Artery Wall</strong>",
                "text": "<p>Your artery walls are a single cell thick — and every day, pressure, blood sugar, and inflammation tear tiny nicks into that lining. Each nick triggers an emergency patch job. That patching isn't healing. It's the first step toward a buildup that doesn't stop.</p>",
                "note": "",
                "align_text": "left"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "tab_QxyXpJ": {
              "type": "_tab",
              "settings": {
                "tab_label": "Stage 2: Cholestrol Gets Deposited",
                "media_type": "image",
                "image": "shopify://shop_images/stage_2_natto.png",
                "show_play_icon": true,
                "video_url": "",
                "autoplay_video": false,
                "heading": "<strong>Stage 2: Cholestrol Gets Deposited</strong>",
                "text": "<p>To patch the damage, your body floods the site with cholesterol. As you age, it piles up faster than your body can clear it — thickening the wall and choking the channel blood actually flows through.</p>",
                "note": "",
                "align_text": "left"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "tab_eaUkTG": {
              "type": "_tab",
              "settings": {
                "tab_label": "Stage 3: Fibrin Locks the Plaque In",
                "media_type": "image",
                "image": "shopify://shop_images/stage_3_natto.png",
                "show_play_icon": true,
                "video": "shopify://files/videos/181f56faf09c46e691d3da577b6537e2.HD-1080p-2.5Mbps-79987212.mp4",
                "video_url": "",
                "autoplay_video": false,
                "heading": "<strong>Stage 3: Fibrin Locks the Plaque In</strong>",
                "text": "<p>Fibrin, a sticky protein, cements the cholesterol and debris into hardened plaque — sealing the buildup permanently into your artery walls. This is the exact buildup nattokinase has been clinically studied to break down.</p>",
                "note": "",
                "align_text": "left"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "tab_Kgt9t4": {
              "type": "_tab",
              "settings": {
                "tab_label": "Stage 4: Blood Flow Restriction",
                "media_type": "image",
                "image": "shopify://shop_images/stage_4_natto.png",
                "show_play_icon": true,
                "video_url": "",
                "autoplay_video": false,
                "heading": "<strong>Stage 4: Blood Flow Restriction</strong>",
                "text": "<p>With the channel choked by plaque, circulation drops — fast. Less oxygen reaches your tissues, and your body starts paying the price: fatigue, cold hands and feet, and rising pressure as your heart works overtime just to keep up.</p>",
                "note": "",
                "align_text": "left"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "tab_L3BGAK": {
              "type": "_tab",
              "settings": {
                "tab_label": "Stage 5: A Clot Can Seal It Off",
                "media_type": "image",
                "image": "shopify://shop_images/stage_5_natto.png",
                "show_play_icon": true,
                "video_url": "",
                "autoplay_video": false,
                "heading": "<strong>Stage 5: A Clot Can Seal It Off</strong>",
                "text": "<p>Plaque can rupture, and a clot forms at the break. If that clot blocks the artery, blood flow stops — which is why keeping arterial buildup in check matters.</p>",
                "note": "",
                "align_text": "left"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "tab_HmVGNt",
            "tab_QxyXpJ",
            "tab_eaUkTG",
            "tab_Kgt9t4",
            "tab_L3BGAK"
          ]
        }
      },
